#
# Per-directory .gitignore for `deploy/secrets/`.
#
# The sops+age scheme (PR #119) keeps encrypted
# secrets IN the repo and the plaintext OUT. The
# plaintext NEVER reaches the repo under any
# circumstance — it lives only on the operator's
# local machine before encryption.
#
# Patterns below are in addition to the root
# `.gitignore`, which catches `age.key`,
# `age-*.key`, and the `*.key` / `*.pem` shapes
# globally.

# Plaintext: NEVER committed. The operator runs
# `sops --encrypt --in-place deploy/secrets/secrets.yml`
# to rewrite the file in-place with the ciphertext;
# the filename stays `secrets.yml` but the content
# shifts from plaintext to sops-format. Anything
# that LOOKS like a plaintext secrets file must
# not commit.
secrets.yml
secrets.local.yml
secrets.*.local.yml

# Permitted: the committed example file (which is
# always encrypted — sops rewrites the example
# in-place during PR preparation too, so the file
# is never plaintext on the main branch). The `!`
# prefix overrides the directory's broad `*` deny
# if any.
!secrets.example.yml

# README + this file (committed).
!README.md
!.gitignore
